{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/946818-some-general-questions","id":946818,"title":"Some general questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-09T02:18:17-07:00","id":946818,"title":"Some general questions","content":"1)Ephemeral entities, Open condition, Reaching<br /> A)Open condition<br /> Can they apply it by themselves on a living subkect, or does the &quot;work in concert with the subject&quot; pretty much means that they need concent?<br /> Example: we have a ghost haunting Bob. Bob is it's murder and anchor, and the ghost has influence 2 over him. Bob is sleeping peacefully with his 2 resolve.<br /> Can the ghost spend 2 scenes rolling, creating the open condition, and proceed to possess bob?<br /> Or is the only way for Bob to be actually possessed to willingly work alongside the ghost so that it can create the Open condition?<br /> <br /> B)Reaching condition<br /> Initially I though that an entity had to be materialized to use numina that don't have the reaching tag.<br /> P.e. a fire spirit materialized and used his numina to cause fire<br /> But some other numina don't make sense.<br /> P.e. sign. A ghost needs to materialize in order to write on a window? It doesn't make sense.<br /> So, the next conclusion was that entities in the twillight form are, in a sense, fully on the fallen world, and thus can use all numina like they were materialized. And that &quot;reaching&quot; is only for using numina over the underworld, the spirit realms, or even astral itself.<br /> Is this correct?<br /> <br /> 2)Matter and equipment bonus<br /> There is already a matter 3 perfecting items in order to give them roll 8 and/or rote quality (perfecting)<br /> There is already matter 2 to shape matter (shaping) in order to make them worse.<br /> I assume that a mage, using the thaumaturgy rules CAN somehow give pure equipment bonus to simple matter items (making a sword super sharp, increasing the mass of a baseball bat, etc), maybe even complex items with reach (and probably a reflexive crafts or science roll).<br /> Does the above makes sense? And if yes, what would it be? Perfecting (Matter 3) or Ruling (Matter 2 like shaping)<br /> <br /> 3)Knocked down tilt.<br /> In it's effect it says that &quot;if the subject hasn't acted yet, it loses his action&quot;<br /> In the resolution it says &quot;if the subject hasn't acted yet it rolls dex+athletics to avoid the tilt&quot;<br /> I assume the resolution is the correct one?<br /> <br /> 4)Adamant Hand, yantra, touch, ordering<br /> A)Casting a spell on a target normally requires a touch (dex+brawl) <br /> Am I correct to assume that if you punch someone (str+brawl) and can cast a reflexive spell (p.e. exceptional luck) on the same turn, you can safely assume that you delivered the spell through the punch and you don't need to &quot;touch him&quot; again?<br /> <br /> B)stacking yantras.<br /> You punch someone with adamant hand, gaining +1 yantra bonus on your next spell cast in subsequent rounds, or to a spell cast reflexively on the same round.<br /> Reflexively you cast exceptional luck.<br /> Can you add your &quot;free&quot; yantra to the mix, or does the +1 from adamant hand counts as the &quot;you may use one yantra reflexively with a spell&quot;?<br /> <br /> C)You hit someone causing the knocked down tilt.<br /> You use exceptional luck reflexively to apply leg wrack.<br /> Does he suffers the -2 to the athletics roll to not fall down, or is this roll made before the spell?<br /> <br /> Big thanks to those who take the time to read through this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11977-shroudb","name":"Shroudb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T02:52:12-07:00","id":946832,"title":"","content":"1.A)<br /> For spirits, the living subject must first be Resonant (they must do things that fits the spirit nature). Afterward, they can then start to make the subject Open with their Influence.<br /> <br /> For ghosts, you are right. The ghost attempts to give Bob the Open condition, and once it has done so, it can directly affect him with what powers that requires it.<br /> <br /> 2.B)<br /> Reaching is only for Spirits or things that want to affect things on the other side of the Gauntlet. I never thought however, that It could also be applied to beings in the Underworld :P<br /> <br /> But you are correct that things in Twilight are in fact, in the psychical world. However, the Signs power doesn't require the entity to be Materialized. But some powers (I think), does require the entity to Materialize.<br /> <br /> 2)<br /> Yes, it should be possible to increase the Weapon rating of the item and I would say it is a Perfecting practice.<br /> <br /> 3)<br /> Both are correct, but I can see why they would be confusing. I'll try and give an example:<br /> <br /> Possessed Bob attempts to apply the Knocked Down Tilt to his &quot;friend&quot; Rod, and is successfully in doing so.<br /> Rod hasn't acted in the turn, so he loses his action for the turn. But, because he hasn't acted, he may attempt a Dexterity + Athletics roll to not be knocked down. He still loses his action, though.<br /> <br /> 4.A)<br /> Not completly sure of the question but I will try. There is no Reflexive Spellcasting in the new addition. Attacking is an Instant action and so is casting a spell, so both can't be done in the same turn.<br /> <br /> 4.B)<br /> As fare as I know, you cannot stack the same Yantras. Normally when using multiple Yantras, you increase the time it take to cast the spell (1 turn for Instant casting and 1 hour for Ritual casting). Adamantin Hand just grants you a &quot;free&quot; Yantra that doesn't increase this time.<br /> <br /> 4.C)<br /> Not sure how casting a dice boosting spell applies the Leg Wrack. But as mentioned, you cannot cast a spell Reflexive anymore.<br /> <br /> But if he was under the hex before the Leg Wrack, he would gain the penalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T03:13:43-07:00","id":946836,"title":"","content":"About 4A<br /> There are some reflexive spells still.<br /> That's why I used exceptional luck.<br /> It has the condition &quot;+2 reach: you cast this spell reflexively &quot;<br /> <br /> About 4B<br /> I didn't mean getting the adamant fist yantra twice. I meant combining adamant fist yantra alongside p.e. another order tool, and effectively using 2 reflexive yantras with a reflexive spell in a turn.<br /> <br /> About 4C<br /> With exceptional luck you can apply a boon or a hex. Hex includes giving specific tilts to targets (as per fate rules), it's not limited just to +/-stats","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11977-shroudb","name":"Shroudb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T03:25:46-07:00","id":946840,"title":"","content":"Aaah, missed that Reach.<br /> <br /> 4.A)<br /> I would guess since the spell is Reflexive that the attack could count as touching the target. However, I don't think you can use Adamant Fist with the spell since hitting someone does symbolically match hexing them to somehow accidentally wrack their arm or leg on a nearby chair.<br /> <br /> 4.B)<br /> The only Reflexive Yantra I've seen is the Adamant Fist. But as I said, the cast time isn't affected when using Adamant Fist. So if Adamant Fist could be used with a Reflexive spell, you could gain 2 Yantras and punch at the same time.<br /> <br /> 4.C) Aah. Got stuck back in first edition when the &quot;boon&quot; or &quot;hex&quot; was just a bonus or penalty to the dice pool. Also, I haven't dabbled so much in Fate :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T03:29:47-07:00","id":946841,"title":"","content":"All spells cast Instantaneously can incorporate one Reflexive Yantra, though some Yantras don't apply, like High Speech.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T03:45:40-07:00","id":946846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/946818-some-general-questions?p=946841#post946841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All spells cast Instantaneously can incorporate one Reflexive Yantra, though some Yantras don't apply, like High Speech.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where does it says it's only for instant spells and not reflexive ones?<br /> The only thing I see in the yantra section is:<br /> &quot;It takes time to draw upon the Supernal sympathy of objects and actions. A mage can draw upon one Yantra as a reflexive action when casting a spell; each further Yantra extends the casting time of instant spells by a turn&quot;<br /> <br /> Edit: just a call out that adamant fist explicitly states that it works with a spell cast reflexively the same round, the question is if you can combine it with the reflexive yantra you get either way when you cast a spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11977,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11977-shroudb","user":"Shroudb","date":". 08-09-2016, 06:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11977-shroudb","name":"Shroudb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T04:20:42-07:00","id":946853,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I was making an implied differentiation between Instant and Ritual. Reflexive get a reflexive Yantra as far as I know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T01:43:23-07:00","id":947605,"title":"","content":"I would say so. There is no rules stating that you can only use one Reflexive thing per turn. So if you have two reflexive Yantras, both should be able to be used in the same turn. Even if the spell that is being cast isn't reflexive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T01:51:42-07:00","id":947610,"title":"","content":"Actually, <i>there is</i> a rule that says that only the first Yantra can be used reflexively, each aditional one takes an aditional turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T03:09:38-07:00","id":947640,"title":"","content":"In the yantra section it is stated, that you can use one yantra reflexively whenever you are casting a spell. The Adamant Hand merit explicitely states that you can use it for reflexive spells in the same turn. So I assume that you can cast a reflexive spell with two yantras (one Adamant Hand, one other) reflexively in the same turn you attacked somebody in a way you got the adamant hand for. As far as I think, this is actually exactly the purpose of Adamant Hand. If you want to use an instant spell in the round after punching somebody, it works exactly the same way (2 reflexive yantras).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T03:13:55-07:00","id":947642,"title":"","content":"It changes something that normally isn't a Yantra into an Order Yantra, it doesn't allow you to break the one reflexive Yantra limit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T00:34:40-07:00","id":948426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/946818-some-general-questions?p=947642#post947642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It changes something that normally isn't a Yantra into an Order Yantra, it doesn't allow you to break the one reflexive Yantra limit.</div> </div> </div> </div>The actual sentence in the Yantra section is: &quot;A mage can draw upon one Yantra as a reflexive action when casting a spell; each further Yantra extends the casting time of instant spells by a turn.&quot;<br /> <br /> And the merit states: &quot;This Merit allows use of that Skill in combat as a reflexive Order tool Yantra, adding dice to a spell cast on subsequent turns, or to a spell cast reflexively in the same turn as the combat action.&quot;<br /> <br /> While I think text of the actual merit might overrule the &quot;only one reflexive yantra&quot;-rule, you may be right. In any case I would lastly house-rule it to stack. Otherwise Adamant Hand is a kind of totally useless merit if basically making a fist as a symbol of conflict can be arguably already work as an order tool. The +1 die to the pool is not really breaking anything and it fits an Arrow playstyle imo if you get a benefit of punching something before spellcasting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T01:49:47-07:00","id":948448,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry, what? In what way is getting to punch something and thus powering your spell, which is how the merit works without house ruling and something Mages without Adamant Hand can't do, how is that useless? I think you're still under some misapprehension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T02:15:46-07:00","id":948457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/946818-some-general-questions?p=948448#post948448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry, what? In what way is getting to punch something and thus powering your spell, which is how the merit works without house ruling and something Mages without Adamant Hand can't do, how is that useless? I think you're still under some misapprehension.</div> </div> </div> </div>what he means, and i agree, is that:<br /> <br /> if the merit doesn't stack with the regular reflexive yantra, then you get absolutely nothing:<br /> <br /> without the merit:<br /> you punch someone<br /> you cast a reflexive spell in the same turn<br /> as per the rules, you are allowed 1 reflexive yantra. let's say you use your fist, your cross, whatever, you get +1 yantra bonus to the spell<br /> EVERY mage can do the above<br /> <br /> <br /> with the merit:<br /> you punch someone<br /> you cast a reflexive spell in the same turn<br /> as per the rules, you are allowed 1 reflexive yantra. let's say you use your fist, your cross, whatever, you get +1 yantra bonus to the spell<br /> IF the merit doesn't allow you to stack, then you get no benefit at all, which is counterintuitive to the fact that the spell specifically works with reflexive spells cast the same round.\u200b<br /> But, if we go by logic, and allow it to stack, then Adamant hand basically gives a +1 casting bonus to the Adamantine arrow as long as they actively attack something each/every other turn<br /> <br /> btw, neither is a house rule, both are interpetations of the actual rule.<br /> <br /> btw, now that i think about it:<br /> isn't EVERY use of the merit a reflexive one?<br /> I mean, you don't need to have predetermined what spell you want to cast (you punch someone, next round, you heal/attack/teleport/whatever and get the merit bonus), so for certain you haven't created an imago at the time of the attack, so for certain you haven't even begin to cast a spell.<br /> <br /> that means, by definition, that when you cast the spell, even if it's the next round, it is at that point that you use the merit benefit and gain its yantra bonus. So, since the action is already &quot;cast a spell&quot;, action economy dictates that the yantra usage is not an &quot;action&quot; but rather something you do reflexively.<br /> <br /> So, if every use of the merit is reflexive, and if you are only allowed 1 reflexive yantra per spell, and you get that either way just because...<br /> <br /> then if they don't stack (as 2 reflexive yantras per turn) then the merit does aboslutly nothing in ANY occasion","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11977,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11977-shroudb","user":"Shroudb","date":". 08-11-2016, 05:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11977-shroudb","name":"Shroudb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T02:41:37-07:00","id":948463,"title":"","content":"There was a discussion about Adamant Hand a while back, IIRC the consensus was: Turn 1, punch; Turn 2, use punch as Yantra without limiting the one Yantra/turn rule, as the necessary action was spent last round.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T02:51:32-07:00","id":948467,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11977-shroudb\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11977\" data-vbnamecard=\"11977\">Shroudb</a> Yes, using the only ability that lets you punch someone in the face and use that to power your spells is doing nothing at all. Adamant Hand doesn't increase the number of Reflexive Yantras you can use, it expands your options for what can be used as a Reflexive Yantra. That is significantly more than doing nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T03:41:55-07:00","id":948483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/946818-some-general-questions?p=948467#post948467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11977-shroudb\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11977\" data-vbnamecard=\"11977\">Shroudb</a> Yes, using the only ability that lets you punch someone in the face and use that to power your spells is doing nothing at all. Adamant Hand doesn't increase the number of Reflexive Yantras you can use, it expands your options for what can be used as a Reflexive Yantra. That is significantly more than doing nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>how? ALL adamantine arrows can use weapon as an order tool. So, &quot;adamantine hand &quot;weaponry&quot; doesn't expand anything. it's the inherent ability of ALL adamantine arrows. You don't even have the limitation of having to use it on the previous round!*<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/946818-some-general-questions?p=948463#post948463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was a discussion about Adamant Hand a while back, IIRC the consensus was: Turn 1, punch; Turn 2, use punch as Yantra without limiting the one Yantra/turn rule, as the necessary action was spent last round.</div> </div> </div> </div>can you point me to the discussion?<br /> if it stacks on the next round, then it should 100% stack on the same round (since both are used as reflexive on the same round in both occasions)<br /> <br /> *edit:<br /> to put it more simple:<br /> ALL order tools can be used reflexively (once per round) without any merit at all.<br /> a punch, a kick, a sword strike, they are all order tools for adamantine arrows<br /> so, by default, any adamantine arrow can use them, as reflexively, once per spell, as order tools.<br /> <br /> so, if the merit doesn't stack, it really does nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11977,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11977-shroudb","user":"Shroudb","date":". 08-11-2016, 06:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11977-shroudb","name":"Shroudb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T03:59:22-07:00","id":948489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shroudb</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/946818-some-general-questions?p=948483#post948483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">can you point me to the discussion?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming\">Here you go.</a><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T04:00:24-07:00","id":948490,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but without adamant hand you can't use a weaponry or weaponry -roll- as a Yantra. You do not get to injure someone and then use that to power your spell. You just brandish your weapon or fist, you don't actually put it to work. I have no idea how you don't see such an obvious difference. Note use of the appropriate -Skill- as a Yantra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 08-11-2016, 07:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T04:27:17-07:00","id":948509,"title":"","content":"A nice thing is that with Adamant Hand, you Punching People in a face is actively related to doing and performing magic (it's a yantra, after all), so it shouldn't suffer from -2 Penalty accrued from Active Mage Sighting. <br /> At least that's how I make it worthwile - Arrows get to perform their combat moves while mage sighting, often forcing you to either drop the Sight or take unfavorable rolls they provoke that suffer from Mage Sight penalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T04:35:16-07:00","id":948514,"title":"","content":"Forgot about that, but yeah that's another benefit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T05:07:30-07:00","id":948523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/946818-some-general-questions?p=948490#post948490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but without adamant hand you can't use a weaponry or weaponry -roll- as a Yantra. You do not get to injure someone and then use that to power your spell. You just brandish your weapon or fist, you don't actually put it to work. I have no idea how you don't see such an obvious difference. Note use of the appropriate -Skill- as a Yantra.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> there is NO difference. Look at my example.<br /> <br /> WITHOUT the merit:<br /> An ordinary adamantine arrow wants to cast spell X<br /> Since weapons are an order tool, he uses his sword as his free, reflexive yantra.<br /> He gets +1 yantra bonus to spell X<br /> <br /> WITH the merit:<br /> The adamantine arrow wants to cast spell X<br /> Since weapons are an order tool, he uses his sword as his free, reflexive yantra.<br /> He gets +1 yantra bonus to spell X<br /> according to you, he can, <b>instead</b>, IF he had previously attacked, to use the same weapon, to get the same +1 bonus (you don't get your -skill- as a bonus, you use your skill as an ORDER tool (+1))<br /> <br /> It offers NOTHING to the adamantine arrows since they get to use weapons as reflexive order tools for free either way, like ALL mages using their ORDER tools.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/946818-some-general-questions?p=948509#post948509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A nice thing is that with Adamant Hand, you Punching People in a face is actively related to doing and performing magic (it's a yantra, after all), so it shouldn't suffer from -2 Penalty accrued from Active Mage Sighting.<br /> At least that's how I make it worthwile - Arrows get to perform their combat moves while mage sighting, often forcing you to either drop the Sight or take unfavorable rolls they provoke that suffer from Mage Sight penalty.</div> </div> </div> </div>that's even more far fetched than simply stacking the bonuses. Because you can use the movements taught by the arrows in their combat training you get to &quot;see&quot; better?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11977,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11977-shroudb","user":"Shroudb","date":". 08-11-2016, 08:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11977-shroudb","name":"Shroudb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T05:25:48-07:00","id":948528,"title":"","content":"Holding your sword and using it are two completely different things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T05:31:23-07:00","id":948531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/946818-some-general-questions?p=948528#post948528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Holding your sword and using it are two completely different things.</div> </div> </div> </div>correctly:<br /> using it it's more restictive AND it's the requirement of the merit<br /> simply holding it (not EVEN holding it, you can have it stashed in your person), it's easier, and you get it for free<br /> <br /> ok, so Dave says this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/886143-2e-adamant-hand-is-underwhelming?p=886248#post886248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Unfortunately the aim roll comes after you've cast, so.. No.<br /> <br /> The main use of Hand is that where every other mage has to stop fighting and rely on their normal Defense while casting spells that take more than one turn, an Arrow can fight and Dodge all she likes - and even use them as yantras.</div> </div> </div> </div>he is effectively says they stack 100% with the normal reflexive one yantra if cast on a seperate round. His dispproval of the example is due to the aimed spell ordering, but if the spell itself is a reflexive one, used in the same round as the spell, then there is nothing stopping you from using both the merit and the ordinary reflexive yantra.<br /> <br /> thanx for the link Justin<br /> <br /> the secondary thing he implies, but I'm not seeing it in the merit description AT ALL, is that you can fight and p.e. cast a spell that requires more mana than what you can spend/turn (like i can use 2 mana, i start casting a spell requiring 3 mana, and i can still attack/dodge on the first round instead of standing still), to be exact, the phrase &quot;and even use them as yantras&quot; points like this is an extra benefit on top of what the merit normally grants you, unlike it being the primary purpose of the merit.<br /> <br /> a bit clarification wouldn't hurt Dave.<br /> Please? ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11977,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11977-shroudb","user":"Shroudb","date":". 08-11-2016, 08:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11977-shroudb","name":"Shroudb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T05:48:41-07:00","id":948539,"title":"","content":"Our point is: you can do exactly the same Adamant Hand does without it, if it does not either stack with the one regular reflexive Yantra or stacks with itself, like ppl in the other thread discussed.<br /> <br /> Example:<br /> <br /> 1. I am an Adamantine Arrow good at knife fighting. I slash at my opponent with the knife, then use the slashing via Adamant Hand as a +1 Yantra to fuel an reflexive Exeptional Luck spell for next round.<br /> 2. I am an Adamantine Arrow good at knife fighting. I slash at my opponent with the knife. Then I cast a reflexive Exeptional Luck spell, using the knife in my hand as a reflexive +1 Order Tool yantra.<br /> <br /> Same effect, but for the first I paid two merit dots.<br /> <br /> I do like the idea of stacking the Adamant Hand Yantras from the other thread though. And it would be in line with what Dave wrote. The Arrow can punsh you for 3 rounds and then use all three punches as individual Yantras to help his spell in the fourth round. But that would also break the &quot;you can only use one reflexive Yantra at all&quot;-rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}